1233
00:49:48,018 --> 00:49:50,755
california, colorado, texas.

1234
00:49:50,788 --> 00:49:52,323
Uh, connecticut.

1235
00:49:52,357 --> 00:49:55,127
- Even this small locust
will attack a man.
- Little bastard.

1236
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:56,495
It has two powerful jaws

1237
00:49:56,528 --> 00:49:57,862
with a ridge full
of sharp teeth.

1238
00:49:57,895 --> 00:49:59,363
And they're vicious gossips.

1239
00:49:59,397 --> 00:50:00,765
And they'll kill other insects
and devour them.

1240
00:50:00,798 --> 00:50:03,135
If no other insects
are available,

1241
00:50:03,168 --> 00:50:04,502
it becomes a cannibal,

1242
00:50:04,535 --> 00:50:06,037
turning on its own kind.

1243
00:50:06,070 --> 00:50:07,472
She wants me.

1244
00:50:07,505 --> 00:50:11,142
What in the good god
are you talking about?

1245
00:50:11,175 --> 00:50:13,778
Now, you've seen
what the locusts can do
in its normal size,

1246
00:50:13,812 --> 00:50:15,180
smaller than your thumb.

1247
00:50:15,213 --> 00:50:16,615
Imagine, if you will,

1248
00:50:16,648 --> 00:50:18,250
a locust that's grown
bigger than a man

1249
00:50:18,283 --> 00:50:19,717
and is continuing to grow,

1250
00:50:19,750 --> 00:50:21,420
some larger than others,
but each one a deadly killer.

1251
00:50:21,453 --> 00:50:22,687
I think it'll go
something like this.

1252
00:50:22,720 --> 00:50:25,323
I hope you realize
we haven't much time.

1253
00:50:25,357 --> 00:50:27,192
You are a scientist,
mr. Wainwright.

1254
00:50:27,225 --> 00:50:28,893
You know what locusts can do.

1255
00:50:28,927 --> 00:50:31,663
- I'm a soldier.
I know what guns can do.
- Together we could...

1256
00:50:31,697 --> 00:50:33,398
I feel secure the illinois
national guard

1257
00:50:33,432 --> 00:50:34,800
can handle this situation.

1258
00:50:34,833 --> 00:50:36,902
Just like they handled
the chicago convention.

1259
00:50:36,935 --> 00:50:39,570
You want to say something,
general hanson?

1260
00:50:39,603 --> 00:50:41,640
- No, sir.
- I'm deeply ashamed.

1261
00:50:41,673 --> 00:50:44,175
I was greatly impressed
with your presentation,
wainwright.

1262
00:50:44,208 --> 00:50:45,743
I'm sure all of us were.

1263
00:50:45,777 --> 00:50:47,078
Thank you very much
for coming.

1264
00:50:47,112 --> 00:50:48,580
Go in peace and say no more.

1265
00:50:48,613 --> 00:50:49,815
I'm afraid my presentation

1266
00:50:49,848 --> 00:50:51,215
didn't impress you
quite enough, general.

1267
00:50:51,248 --> 00:50:53,218
I don't understand you.

1268
00:50:53,252 --> 00:50:55,353
I mean, that when
the locusts start to move
out of that forest,

1269
00:50:55,387 --> 00:50:57,022
I'm not sure you'll be able
to stop them.

1270
00:50:57,055 --> 00:50:59,557
What are you suggesting we do,
mr. Wainwright?

1271
00:50:59,590 --> 00:51:01,593
Hit them with everything
you've got now.

1272
00:51:01,627 --> 00:51:02,960
You need more men,
a lot more men.

1273
00:51:02,993 --> 00:51:04,495
You need tanks
and heavy artillery.

1274
00:51:04,528 --> 00:51:07,365
As of now the full strength
of the illinois national guard

1275
00:51:07,398 --> 00:51:09,868
is in the line, surrounding
the ludlow national forest.

1276
00:51:09,902 --> 00:51:11,002
Go away now.

1277
00:51:11,035 --> 00:51:12,137
As I said before,
mr. Wainwright,

1278
00:51:12,170 --> 00:51:13,438
you are a scientist.

1279
00:51:13,472 --> 00:51:15,407
Why not leave the fighting
to the military?

1280
00:51:15,440 --> 00:51:18,777
Did you just call me a wussy?

1281
00:51:18,810 --> 00:51:21,780
Well, guess I'll just leave you
a few of my brochures.

1282
00:51:21,813 --> 00:51:24,082
No, that's fine.
Thank you.

1283
00:51:24,115 --> 00:51:27,418
Urgent call from paxton,
illinois, sir.

1284
00:51:29,955 --> 00:51:31,857
Here, you talk in this end,
sir.

1285
00:51:31,890 --> 00:51:34,860
- General short here.
- General shorthair?

1286
00:51:34,893 --> 00:51:38,197
I don't know, stuffing.
Whatever you make.

1287
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:41,767
[Muffled]
Help us, general...

1288
00:51:41,800 --> 00:51:44,002
Help, please.

1289
00:51:44,035 --> 00:51:46,303
You will fly to paxton
with mr. Wainwright.

1290
00:51:46,337 --> 00:51:47,738
You'll take charge
of operations.

1291
00:51:47,772 --> 00:51:49,340
Hey, I'm vindicated.
How many dead?

1292
00:51:49,373 --> 00:51:51,877
Wainwright,
I owe you an apology.

1293
00:51:51,910 --> 00:51:54,478
The locusts have broken
through our defense line.

1294
00:51:54,512 --> 00:51:56,280
Thousands of casualties.

1295
00:51:56,313 --> 00:51:57,682
Our troops are reorganizing

1296
00:51:57,715 --> 00:52:00,085
to prevent paxton itself
from being overrun.

1297
00:52:00,118 --> 00:52:02,320
I'm trying not to laugh, sir.

1298
00:52:02,353 --> 00:52:04,322
♪♪ [Humming
raiders of the lost ark theme]

1299
00:52:05,990 --> 00:52:08,927
The hill position
in the suburbs of paxton
must be held.

1300
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:10,795
Otherwise the 100 miles

1301
00:52:10,828 --> 00:52:12,130
between paxton and chicago
will lie open.

1302
00:52:12,163 --> 00:52:14,098
Can I get some nuts?

1303
00:52:14,132 --> 00:52:17,068
[Man on intercom]
General, we can't land in
paxton, sir.

1304
00:52:17,102 --> 00:52:18,203
Why not?

1305
00:52:18,237 --> 00:52:20,072
It just came over the radio,
sir.

1306
00:52:20,105 --> 00:52:23,875
Giant locusts have overrun
paxton at 1400.

1307
00:52:25,743 --> 00:52:28,313
[Muffled]
I told you so.

1308
00:52:28,347 --> 00:52:29,447
Head for chicago.

1309
00:52:29,480 --> 00:52:30,915
Yes, sir.

1310
00:52:30,948 --> 00:52:33,252
Well, no more lunches
at milda's cafe, huh?

1311
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:44,662
"Dear abby, I'm an elderly
woman who doesn't enjoy se--"

1312
00:52:44,695 --> 00:52:46,565
oh, this came
to the wrong place.

1313
00:52:46,598 --> 00:52:48,233
Captain,
I want these positions held,

1314
00:52:48,267 --> 00:52:49,367
and I want them held
at all costs,

1315
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:51,135
if humanly possible.

1316
00:52:51,168 --> 00:52:54,005
Captain, have your map people
immediately turn out over
300 overlays

1317
00:52:54,038 --> 00:52:58,108
showing
the chicago defense line...

1318
00:52:58,142 --> 00:52:59,912
Yes?

1319
00:52:59,945 --> 00:53:03,582
Thank you,
sergeant whisper thin.

1320
00:53:03,615 --> 00:53:06,685
Yes, nothing gets tobacco juice
out of your clothes.

1321
00:53:10,788 --> 00:53:13,458
Boy, I read slow.

1322
00:53:13,492 --> 00:53:14,692
Major everett...

1323
00:53:14,725 --> 00:53:16,995
Our road trip to peoria
has been cancelled.

1324
00:53:17,028 --> 00:53:18,830
- How about squadron 12?
- They haven't reported in yet,
general.

1325
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:19,830
Let me know
the moment you hear.

1326
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:21,065
Yes, sir.

1327
00:53:21,098 --> 00:53:22,800
- I'll be with you in a moment.
- Okay, son.

1328
00:53:22,833 --> 00:53:24,602
Bill, you'll proceed at once

1329
00:53:24,635 --> 00:53:27,105
to temporary ghq central sector
and assume command.

1330
00:53:27,138 --> 00:53:29,807
- ROBERT FROST.
- YOU WILL ORDER THE 81st
ARMORED DIVISION

1331
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:31,208
to proceed without delay

1332
00:53:31,242 --> 00:53:32,577
to fort sheridan in chicago.

1333
00:53:32,610 --> 00:53:34,145
Have the cg report to me
upon arrival.

1334
00:53:34,178 --> 00:53:35,580
And get this man an arm.

1335
00:53:35,613 --> 00:53:37,515
...the defense department to
alert the following divisions--

1336
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:41,052
THE FIRST ARMORED,
THE 40th, THE FIRST AIRBORNE,

1337
00:53:41,085 --> 00:53:43,422
THE 92nd AND THE 76th.

1338
00:53:43,455 --> 00:53:44,422
Okay, any salad with that?

1339
00:53:44,455 --> 00:53:45,923
Uh, what's your problem?

1340
00:53:45,957 --> 00:53:49,227
At the rate refuges are pouring
into chicago, general,

1341
00:53:49,260 --> 00:53:51,830
our emergency staff
won't last long.

1342
00:53:51,863 --> 00:53:54,967
Then we'll feed them crickets.
Yeah. That's it.

1343
00:53:55,000 --> 00:53:57,068
Ech, now, why did I do that?

1344
00:54:00,438 --> 00:54:02,373
Toxaphene is one
we haven't tried.

1345
00:54:02,407 --> 00:54:03,542
How good is it?

1346
00:54:03,575 --> 00:54:04,775
Almost as powerful
as chlordane.

1347
00:54:04,808 --> 00:54:06,177
With no after taste.

1348
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:08,178
All right, ship 2,000 gallons
out to the base.

1349
00:54:08,212 --> 00:54:10,448
- Take a pint for yourself.
- Excuse me.

1350
00:54:10,482 --> 00:54:13,418
[Phone rings]

1351
00:54:13,452 --> 00:54:14,987
- Hello.
- Bat lab.

1352
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:16,020
Speaking.

1353
00:54:16,053 --> 00:54:18,823
Squadron 12 just reported.

1354
00:54:18,857 --> 00:54:21,125
They say they came down
in the day

1355
00:54:21,158 --> 00:54:23,795
and practically drowned
the enemy in insecticide.

1356
00:54:23,828 --> 00:54:25,097
I just got a haircut,
and it hurts.

1357
00:54:25,130 --> 00:54:26,563
The chlordane didn't even
slow them down.

1358
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:28,600
They threw it back at me
and laughed.

1359
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:30,102
We'll have to come up
with something stronger.

1360
00:54:30,135 --> 00:54:32,503
I'll do my best, general.

1361
00:54:32,537 --> 00:54:34,038
Good-bye.

1362
00:54:34,072 --> 00:54:36,540
How about chlordane
with a tiny drop of retsin?

1363
00:54:36,573 --> 00:54:38,075
It's no good.
Forget it.

1364
00:54:38,108 --> 00:54:39,677
Doesn't cause
enough birth defects.

1365
00:54:41,980 --> 00:54:43,915
What else
can I do around here?

1366
00:54:43,948 --> 00:54:45,250
Make myself useful.

1367
00:54:47,818 --> 00:54:49,720
Ah, here we go.

1368
00:54:49,753 --> 00:54:52,290
Oh, no, new petitions
against tax again?

1369
00:54:52,323 --> 00:54:55,260
Dear god.

1370
00:54:55,293 --> 00:54:56,293
Looks pretty bad, doesn't it?

1371
00:54:56,327 --> 00:54:57,328
No, you look fine.

1372
00:54:57,362 --> 00:54:58,697
Thought you went back
to new york?

1373
00:54:58,730 --> 00:55:00,865
Well, the big story is here.

1374
00:55:00,898 --> 00:55:03,802
Look, your editor called
you back because it was
too dangerous.

1375
00:55:03,835 --> 00:55:08,338
I wanted to be here.

1376
00:55:08,372 --> 00:55:10,275
Nothing we've done so far--

1377
00:55:10,308 --> 00:55:12,143
insecticides, fire bombs,

1378
00:55:12,177 --> 00:55:14,712
nothing has done any good.

1379
00:55:14,745 --> 00:55:16,380
And so little time.

1380
00:55:16,413 --> 00:55:18,315
Well, you're doing
everything you can.

1381
00:55:18,348 --> 00:55:21,518
Everybody is,
but it's not good enough.

1382
00:55:21,552 --> 00:55:23,287
Maybe if I try to toss
a quarter into that thing.

1383
00:55:23,320 --> 00:55:26,323
In time the beasts
will inherit the earth.

1384
00:55:26,357 --> 00:55:28,493
There's your answer!
A fine pilsner!

1385
00:55:32,597 --> 00:55:37,002
Lee marvin in the bridges
of madison county.

1386
00:55:37,035 --> 00:55:38,770
♪♪ [Humming]

1387
00:55:42,773 --> 00:55:44,708
Hey, general, where you going?

1388
00:55:44,742 --> 00:55:47,945
I'm going to decatur!
I'm gonna shoot that
paper-hanging son of a bitch!

1389
00:55:50,282 --> 00:55:51,382
[Death rattles]

1390
00:55:51,415 --> 00:55:52,583
Sorry about that. Sorry.

1391
00:55:54,285 --> 00:55:59,290
Well, I guess wait till the
grasshoppers show up, huh?

1392
00:55:59,323 --> 00:56:01,425
All quiet
in the western suburbs.

1393
00:56:07,498 --> 00:56:09,833
There's no sign of the locusts
yet, general.

1394
00:56:09,867 --> 00:56:11,168
Out.

1395
00:56:11,202 --> 00:56:13,772
Should we just continue
firing at random?

1396
00:56:15,973 --> 00:56:19,810
The jack benny program.

1397
00:56:19,843 --> 00:56:22,247
And with the lock
of five divisions
to the western south...

1398
00:56:22,280 --> 00:56:23,782
Mr. Mitchell.

1399
00:56:23,815 --> 00:56:25,117
General hanson is confident

1400
00:56:25,150 --> 00:56:26,785
that he can keep the menace
at bay.

1401
00:56:26,818 --> 00:56:28,185
That's dennis the menace.

1402
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,053
The air force and marines
are moving into position.

1403
00:56:30,087 --> 00:56:34,092
To back up those forces
already deployed by the army.

1404
00:56:34,125 --> 00:56:36,995
The one advantage our forces
hold over the enemy...

1405
00:56:37,028 --> 00:56:38,128
Don't sit so close, dear.

1406
00:56:38,162 --> 00:56:39,563
...always reveal
their intention to attack.

1407
00:56:39,597 --> 00:56:40,732
Which is nice.

1408
00:56:40,765 --> 00:56:42,333
Before every attack,

1409
00:56:42,367 --> 00:56:44,068
the locusts send forth
this warning

1410
00:56:44,102 --> 00:56:46,337
in the form
of a high-pitched screech.

1411
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:49,607
Looks like the sun king's bell
on top of their tv

1412
00:56:49,640 --> 00:56:52,077
until it reaches
ear shattering proportions.

1413
00:56:52,110 --> 00:56:53,478
Sounds like mariah carey.

1414
00:56:53,512 --> 00:56:55,480
The screech reaches
its full intensity

1415
00:56:55,513 --> 00:56:58,382
when the locusts attack.

1416
00:56:58,415 --> 00:57:00,518
Copy.

1417
00:57:00,552 --> 00:57:02,887
We've got every available man
on the line, major,

1418
00:57:02,920 --> 00:57:04,955
and I think there's no question
but what will be.

1419
00:57:04,988 --> 00:57:06,892
- [Chirping]
- Hush now.

1420
00:57:06,925 --> 00:57:13,532
Oh, I love a spring rain.

1421
00:57:13,565 --> 00:57:15,467
I shouldn't have worn
my butt dress.

1422
00:57:18,570 --> 00:57:20,372
Oh, great, they're early.

1423
00:57:20,405 --> 00:57:22,207
[Clamoring]

1424
00:57:22,240 --> 00:57:27,112
The cubs don't win the pennant!
The cubs don't win the pennant!

1425
00:57:27,145 --> 00:57:29,913
Meanwhile,
at the boy scout jamboree
at pottawattomie park...

1426
00:57:32,350 --> 00:57:33,852
I wanna drive your tank.

1427
00:57:33,885 --> 00:57:35,487
I call the front.

1428
00:57:37,222 --> 00:57:38,590
Oh, so far seems pretty--

1429
00:57:38,623 --> 00:57:40,392
oh, my god, look out!

1430
00:57:40,425 --> 00:57:41,525
Hold your fire, men.

1431
00:57:41,558 --> 00:57:42,727
We'll negotiate!

1432
00:57:42,760 --> 00:57:44,362
Cricket lighter.

1433
00:57:44,395 --> 00:57:46,530
Just $1.49.

1434
00:57:51,002 --> 00:57:52,503
- Wow.
- Oh, I'm hit.

1435
00:57:52,537 --> 00:57:56,875
They got jiminy!
Get 'em!

1436
00:57:56,908 --> 00:57:58,275
We were pinned
down near elgin.

1437
00:57:58,308 --> 00:58:00,478
Aurora was pretty bad.

1438
00:58:00,512 --> 00:58:02,980
Bad, it stunk in there.

1439
00:58:03,013 --> 00:58:04,682
Whoo, sweat lodge.

1440
00:58:07,018 --> 00:58:10,053
Okay, okay. Okay, gotcha!

1441
00:58:12,490 --> 00:58:17,395
Whoops. Oh, I'm sorry.
Let me clear the shot.

1442
00:58:17,428 --> 00:58:19,230
This is where you step back

1443
00:58:19,263 --> 00:58:21,665
and say, thank god
for my exoskeleton.

1444
00:58:23,533 --> 00:58:25,403
[Muffled]
This is flying officer
jim cavanaugh.

1445
00:58:25,437 --> 00:58:27,405
The dan ryan's covered with
tobacco juice.

1446
00:58:27,438 --> 00:58:29,407
You might want to try an
alternate route.

1447
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:32,210
Let's all welcome bob hope,
ladies and gentlemen.

1448
00:58:34,978 --> 00:58:37,115
Even out best footage
can't stop them!

1449
00:58:39,183 --> 00:58:41,052
Have you seen
my mommy and daddy?

1450
00:58:41,085 --> 00:58:43,153
[Crying]

1451
00:58:43,187 --> 00:58:47,392
Damn nazi grasshoppers.

1452
00:58:47,425 --> 00:58:49,560
Hi, I'm going to sneak
in here to say,

1453
00:58:49,593 --> 00:58:50,962
"hope you're enjoying
the show.

1454
00:58:50,995 --> 00:58:52,097
Bye for now."

1455
00:58:52,130 --> 00:58:53,832
Ho, I've got a great gun.

1456
00:58:53,865 --> 00:58:55,367
No, I don't need a bazooka.

1457
00:58:58,737 --> 00:59:02,440
The orkin army will storm
the beaches of lake forest.

1458
00:59:04,542 --> 00:59:06,277
We're going to have to get
organized.

1459
00:59:06,310 --> 00:59:08,780
We should not be losing
to grasshoppers, people.

1460
00:59:16,387 --> 00:59:20,492
So is this protecting chicago
at all costs, sir?

1461
00:59:20,525 --> 00:59:22,460
They keep coming, general.

1462
00:59:22,493 --> 00:59:25,930
They're lobbing aphids at us!

1463
00:59:25,963 --> 00:59:27,965
They're hammering at a single
point in our line.

1464
00:59:27,998 --> 00:59:29,867
I don't know how,
but they've arranged air cover

1465
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:31,235
from the mexican army.

1466
00:59:31,268 --> 00:59:33,772
They cut off our supply lines
and ate the radio men.

1467
00:59:38,042 --> 00:59:40,478
No grasshoppers were hurt
in the making of this film,
huh?

1468
00:59:42,713 --> 00:59:45,617
I don't believe it!
They're using hannibal's
surprise!

1469
00:59:50,822 --> 00:59:53,023
They keep coming, general.

1470
00:59:53,057 --> 00:59:55,058
They're moving closer.

1471
00:59:55,092 --> 00:59:57,195
Still they come,
wave after wave.

1472
00:59:57,228 --> 00:59:58,595
They've broken our code,

1473
00:59:58,628 --> 01:00:00,565
and the sergeant
was a grasshopper under cover.

1474
01:00:02,167 --> 01:00:05,102
[Mumbling]
...Coming.

1475
01:00:05,135 --> 01:00:07,372
They're pouring through
a breach in our lines.

1476
01:00:07,405 --> 01:00:10,775
We're being cut off!

1477
01:00:10,808 --> 01:00:12,143
